# datapy.os — Cursor AI Rules
# ==============================
# These rules give Cursor complete context. Read before writing any code.

## Project identity
DataPy.os is a data-native OS: **data + Python + AI**, not a classical folder tree.
Objects are addressed by OID, flat handles, tags, and links. Collections are
semantic (tags/graph), never parent directories.

Stack:
  Host / Pi / UEFI
    → Python runtime
    → NovaKernel      (kernel/nova.py)
    → DataPlane       (store/dataplane.py)  # secure CRUD — primary surface
    → SOS             (store/sos.py)        # content-addressed SQLite WAL
    → Shell / AI

## Target platforms
- Raspberry Pi 5 (ARM64) — primary, boots from USB
- x86-64 UEFI PC — secondary
- Any machine: `python3 main.py` (dev mode)

## The ONE rule: never touch disk directly
ALWAYS use `sos.write(path, content)` and `sos.read(path)`.
NEVER use `open()` to store data persistently.
The SOS IS the filesystem. SQLite WAL mode, content-addressed, versioned.

## Subsystem map (all on kernel.*)
```
kernel.sos        SemanticObjectStore    store/sos.py
kernel.ai         AIEngine (tiered LLM) ai/engine.py
kernel.shell      NovaShell              shell/nova_shell.py
