kernel.i18n       I18n                   i18n/engine.py
kernel.raft       RaftNode               system/enterprise.py
kernel.compliance ComplianceManager      system/enterprise.py
kernel.cloud      CloudManifests         system/enterprise.py
```

## Adding a shell command (the most common task)
```python
# 1. In shell/nova_shell.py, inside _build_cmds():
"mycommand": self._mycommand_cmd,

# 2. Add the handler method:
def _mycommand_cmd(self, args: list[str]) -> None:
    """mycommand list|add|rm — one-line description."""
    sub = args[0] if args else "list"
    if sub == "list":
        for item in self.kernel.something.list():
            print(f"  {col(item.name,'cyan'):<25} {item.description}")
    elif sub == "add" and len(args) > 1:
        self.kernel.something.add(args[1])
        self._ok(f"Added: {args[1]}")
    else:
        print("  Usage: mycommand list|add <name>|rm <name>")
```

Shell helpers: `self._ok(msg)`, `self._err(msg)`, `col(text, color)`.

## Coding standards
1. Module-level docstring on EVERY .py file (CI enforces 100%)
2. Type annotations on all public functions
3. `from __future__ import annotations` + TYPE_CHECKING for circular imports
4. No bare `except:` — always `except Exception as exc:`
5. `logging.getLogger("nova.module")` not `print()` for logs
6. Line limit: 100 chars. Formatter: ruff.

## SOS quick reference
```python
sos.write(path, content, kind="text", tags=["note"])  # create/update
sos.read(path)           # returns content string
sos.resolve(path)        # returns OID (SHA-256 hex)
sos.exists(path)         # bool
sos.listdir(path)        # list of child names
sos.search("query")      # FTS5 full-text search
sos.find_by_tag("tag")   # returns list of OIDs
sos.mkdir(path)          # create directory node
sos.remove(path)         # soft delete (version retained)
```

## AI engine tiers
1. llama-cpp-python — GGUF model, GPU/CPU, full quality
2. NanoLLM — fast, tiny, embedding-based
3. RAG — retrieval from SOS, always available (NOVA_NO_AI=1 forces this)

```python
response = kernel.ai.ask("query", max_tokens=200)  # auto-selects tier
kernel.ai.tier   # "llama" | "nano" | "rag"
```

