## Run locally
```bash
python3 main.py            # full OS in terminal
python3 main.py --no-ai    # no LLM, fast
python3 main.py --cmd "ls /"
pytest tests/ -v
```

## Build Pi 5 USB image
```bash
python3 build/build_pi5_nova.py   # downloads ~37 MB, outputs nova_pi5.img
# Flash with Rufus → DD Image mode
```

## Environment variables
NOVA_DATA  ~/.nova     SOS database + models directory
NOVA_SRC   auto        Root of datapy.os source tree
NOVA_MODEL auto        Path to GGUF model file
NOVA_NO_AI unset       Set 1 to force RAG tier (fast startup)
NOVA_LOG   info        debug / info / warning / error

## What NOT to do
- NEVER use open() for persistent data — always sos.write()
- NEVER use print() for logging — use logging.getLogger()
- NEVER hardcode ~/.nova paths — use os.environ.get("NOVA_DATA")
- NEVER remove module docstrings (CI gate)
- NEVER add Linux-only syscalls (code runs bare-metal on Pi)
